WEBVTT

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:31.469
Having realized that I'm burnt out,
I recognize burnout behaviors.

00:15:31.493 --> 00:15:34.445
AG: So it seems then that part
of what you like about burnout

00:15:34.469 --> 00:15:37.136
is that it helps you recognize

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.926
that this is a problem
embedded in your circumstances.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.986
As opposed to a problem in your head.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:47.452
AHP: Yeah, that's a great way
of putting it.

00:15:47.476 --> 00:15:50.146
AG: Annie and I landed
on a key distinction.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.506
Burnout isn't just feeling
emotionally exhausted

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.016
for a little while.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.266
It's feeling that way often enough
or intensely enough

00:15:57.290 --> 00:15:59.636
that it starts to interfere
with your functioning,

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.086
even if you don't actually quit.